  "name": "3.10(b) Distribution Account withdrawals",
  "text": "(b) The Trust Administrator shall withdraw funds from the Distribution Account for distributions to Certificateholders, in the manner specified in this Agreement (and withhold from the amounts so withdrawn, the amount of any taxes that it is authorized to withhold pursuant to the last paragraph of Section 9.11). In addition, the Trust Administrator may from time to time make withdrawals from the Distribution Account for the following purposes: 61 of 177 9/28/2010 12:22 PM Exhibit 4.1 http://www.secinfo.com/$/SEC/Filing.asp?H=13f21.v1Hs.d&OS=W (i) to pay to the Trust Administrator earnings on or investment income, if any with respect to funds in or credited to the Distribution Account; (ii) to withdraw and return to the Master Servicer any amount deposited in the Distribution Account and not required to be deposited therein in accordance with Section 3.07(d); (iii) to withdraw any indemnity, expense or other reimbursement owed to it or the Trustee pursuant to this Agreement, including, without limitation, Section 3.05, Section 7.02, Section 8.05 and Section 9.05; (iv) on each Distribution Date, to pay the Credit Risk Manager Fee to the Credit Risk Manager; provided, however, that upon termination of the Credit Risk Manager pursuant to Section 3.26 hereof, the amount of the Credit Risk Manager Fee (or any portion thereof) previously payable to the Credit Risk Manager as described herein shall be paid to the Transferor; and (v) to clear and terminate the Distribution Account upon termination of the Agreement pursuant to Section 10.01 hereof."
},
{
